  "mood": "A gilded masonry beacon revealed by opening copper vaults at violet dusk",
  "reason": "The lantern citadel is carved into a descending stone escarpment rather than placed on a flat lawn. Two thick copper vault leaves open on connected masonry abutments, revealing the tall bay-lit beacon and clustered eaved magenta roofs. A lower architectural viewpoint makes the terraced foreground edge and cool distant ridge carry depth. Rising roof city and rotating bridge alternatives weakened the singular source tower. All geometry, terrain and mechanics are explicitly invented.",
